WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:16.519
The forest came alive with the sound of the boys cutting and hammering.

2
00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:27.094
They had already carried up everything Wendy might need from their underground home—tables, chairs, a dresser, and a bed.

3
00:00:27.095 --> 00:00:30.894
Now they needed to build the walls.

4
00:00:30.895 --> 00:00:35.620
"If only we knew the kind of house she likes," said Curly.

5
00:00:35.621 --> 00:00:44.154
When Wendy began to wake up, they asked, "Wendy, tell us what kind of house you would like."

6
00:00:44.155 --> 00:00:50.754
Opening her eyes, she began to sing:

7
00:00:50.755 --> 00:00:57.603
I wish I had a pretty house, The littlest ever seen,

8
00:00:57.604 --> 00:01:08.943
With funny little red walls And a roof of mossy green.

9
00:01:08.944 --> 00:01:12.016
They were delighted to hear her voice.

10
00:01:12.017 --> 00:01:17.589
They brought moss for the roof, and branches with red sap for the walls of the little house.

11
00:01:17.590 --> 00:01:20.704
"What next?" they asked.

12
00:01:20.705 --> 00:01:25.446
And she sang again:

13
00:01:25.447 --> 00:01:32.503
Oh, next I'll have Blue windows all about,

14
00:01:32.504 --> 00:01:43.958
With roses peeking in, And children peeping out.

15
00:01:43.959 --> 00:01:50.798
They carved out windows and made make-believe roses to decorate the outside of the windows.

16
00:01:50.799 --> 00:01:55.072
As for children, they would be her children.

17
00:01:55.073 --> 00:01:57.875
The house was almost done.

18
00:01:57.876 --> 00:02:03.923
It looked beautiful, and the boys were very proud that they had made such a nice place for her.

19
00:02:03.924 --> 00:02:06.202
They loved Wendy already.

20
00:02:06.203 --> 00:02:11.015
But once the walls were up around her, the boys couldn't see her anymore.

21
00:02:11.016 --> 00:02:14.942
They stayed outside, wondering what to do.

22
00:02:14.943 --> 00:02:21.941
"What we need now is a door and a knocker," said the practical Slightly.

23
00:02:21.942 --> 00:02:25.676
They shaped a door from a large piece of wood.

24
00:02:25.677 --> 00:02:30.823
Then Tootles gave up the bottom of his shoe, which made an excellent knocker.

25
00:02:30.824 --> 00:02:33.956
Now the house was truly finished.

26
00:02:33.957 --> 00:02:37.939
There was nothing to do now but knock on the door.

27
00:02:37.940 --> 00:02:42.241
"We must all look our best," Peter told the boys.

28
00:02:42.242 --> 00:02:45.549
"First impressions are very important."

29
00:02:45.550 --> 00:02:50.079
They washed their hands in a nearby stream and came back to the house.

30
00:02:50.080 --> 00:02:55.085
In the lead as always, Peter knocked politely on the door.

31
00:02:55.086 --> 00:02:58.314
The door opened and Wendy came out.

32
00:02:58.315 --> 00:03:02.950
She looked properly surprised—just how they had hoped she would look.

33
00:03:02.951 --> 00:03:05.880
"Who are you?" she asked.

34
00:03:05.881 --> 00:03:08.490
Slightly was the first to speak.

35
00:03:08.491 --> 00:03:14.462
"Wendy, we are the Lost Boys, and we have built this house for you."

36
00:03:14.463 --> 00:03:20.395
"Oh, say that you're pleased," cried Nibs excitedly.

37
00:03:20.396 --> 00:03:22.776
"It's a very lovely house!

38
00:03:22.777 --> 00:03:27.840
I thank you so much for your kindness," said Wendy.

39
00:03:27.841 --> 00:03:31.618
And that was just what they had hoped she would say.

40
00:03:31.619 --> 00:03:37.955
"And we want to be your children," said Tootles shyly.

41
00:03:37.956 --> 00:03:44.921
Then they all went down on their knees and cried, "Wendy, please be our mother."

42
00:03:44.922 --> 00:03:53.021
"But I'm only a little girl," said Wendy, "and I have no real experience as a mother."

43
00:03:53.022 --> 00:03:57.758
"Doesn't matter," said Peter, who always knew best.

44
00:03:57.759 --> 00:04:02.548
"We just need a nice motherly type of person to help us."

45
00:04:02.549 --> 00:04:06.361
"I will do my best," Wendy replied.

46
00:04:06.362 --> 00:04:12.608
With those words, she invited all the boys, including her brothers, inside.

47
00:04:12.609 --> 00:04:17.208
"Make sure to take off your shoes first," she instructed.

48
00:04:17.209 --> 00:04:20.700
"Then I'll tell you a story before you go to bed.

49
00:04:20.701 --> 00:04:26.080
How would you like it if I told you the rest of the story of Cinderella?"

50
00:04:26.081 --> 00:04:30.677
All the boys were delighted, even John and Michael.

51
00:04:30.678 --> 00:04:33.950
They squeezed into the tiny little house.

52
00:04:33.951 --> 00:04:39.000
And that was the first of many cozy evenings the boys spent with Wendy.

53
00:04:39.001 --> 00:04:45.674
Later, when she felt better, she began to tuck them into their beds in the house underground.

54
00:04:45.675 --> 00:04:51.693
But for quite a long time, she slept in the little house the boys had lovingly made for her.

55
00:04:51.694 --> 00:04:54.877
Peter kept watch outside with his sword.

56
00:04:54.878 --> 00:05:00.966
Pirates, Indians, and beasts could be heard prowling in the distance.

57
00:05:00.967 --> 00:05:10.665
And so they lived happily ever after—for a while.
